# Constitution

Non-negotiable guardrails for every task. Details live in `playwright-conventions.mdc` (`tests/**`) and skills.

## MUST

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Role-based locators (`getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId`+why) | Survives DOM/CSS churn |
| Web-first assertions (`expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, etc.) | Auto-retry; no snapshot booleans |
| `storageState` auth via setup project | No UI login in every feature test |
| Unique, self-cleaning data (`uniqueName`, `trackProgram`, cleanup fixture) | Safe under `fullyParallel` |
| One suite tag per test (`@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, or `@destructive`; never on `describe`) | Traceability; `@destructive` only for shared/global state mutators |

## SHOULD

| Practice | When |
|----------|------|
| Faker factories | Repeated or structured test payloads |
| Enums for repeated strings | Status labels, routes, copy keys |
| JSDoc on POM action methods | Non-obvious flows or side effects |

## WON'T

| Refuse | Do instead |
|--------|------------|
| XPath / CSS selectors | Re-discover via role-based locators |
| `waitForTimeout` | Web-first `expect(locator)` |
| Hardcoded secrets | Env vars, `storageState`, fixtures |
| `any` | Infer or define a proper type |
| Weakened assertions | Fix locator, wait, mock, or file a bug |
| Heal a real app bug | Triage → bug-reporter |
| Tags on `describe` | Tag individual tests only |

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract for the coordinator and subagents — **not hook-enforced**.

### Audit-then-edit

1. **Audit** — read ticket/spec, repo paths, live UI or traces, env docs; list what is verified vs assumed.
2. **Proposal** — for any non-trivial task, emit a Proposal block **before** editing.
3. **Edit** — only after the confidence gate allows it; prefer minimal diffs aligned with this constitution.

Trivial tasks (typo, explicit one-line user instruction with no ambiguity) may skip the Proposal block.

### Proposal block

```
Proposal
- Scope: …
- Confidence: N/10
- Rationale: …
- Unknowns: …
```

| Confidence | Action |
|------------|--------|
| **< 5** | Do **not** proceed — ask for the missing input or explore read-only |
| **5–7** | Proceed only with Unknowns listed explicitly; **wait for human approval** before edits |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed; still state material Unknowns if any remain |

### No fabrication

Never invent a **path**, **enum**, **env var**, **credential**, or **UI message** — ask, read `.env.example` / README / specs, or explore the repo and live app instead. Observed copy and existing conventions beat assumptions.

## Skills & agents

**Skills:** `a11y-checks` (axe on new UI) · `ci-failure-triage` (classify red CI) · `didaxis-bulk-cleanup` (API program purge) · `explore-and-generate` (coverage gaps, no ticket) · `jira-bug-reporter` (failure → Jira) · `jira-ticket-to-gherkin` (AC → plan) · `network-mocked-edge-cases` (`page.route` HTTP edges) · `playwright-test-cleanup` (`trackProgram` teardown) · `pom-conventions` (POM layout) · `self-heal` (drift-only locator repair)

**Agents:** `test-writer` (plan → spec) · `triage` (red run diagnosis) · `bug-reporter` (confirmed app bug → Jira)
